IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cp4-nouns`
IMPORT `cp4-pension-index`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, section 56 -- THE DISABILITY PENSION.
--
-- A disability pension (paragraph 44(1)(b), piece cp3) is a basic monthly amount made of a flat rate
-- benefit and 75% of the contributor's retirement pension, that pension being the aggregate of three
-- portions: 25% of the average monthly pensionable earnings (subsection (3)), 8.33% of the first
-- additional monthly pensionable earnings (subsection (3.1)) and 33.33% of the second additional
-- monthly pensionable earnings (subsection (3.2)). Subsections (4), (4.01), (4.02) and (4.1) say how
-- those earnings are averaged, subsection (5) says what the contributory period is for that purpose,
-- and subsection (6) re-weighs the base portion when a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings
-- changes it.
--
-- Out of range, taken as plain inputs: the Pension Index (s 43, piece cp3); the contributor's total
-- pensionable earnings, total first and second additional pensionable earnings and additional
-- contributory periods (ss 49.1, 49.2, 50 to 50.2, piece cp3); the deductions that subsections 48(2)
-- and (4) allow (piece cp3); the dates of subsection 42(2) (piece cp3); the family allowance recipient
-- months (s 42(1) and reg 77, pieces cp3 and cr2).

§ `Section 56 -- amount of disability pension`

§§ `The earnings a disability pension is worked out from`

-- Facts that subsections (4) and (4.1) read, each worked out by another section.
-- Subsections 48(2) and (4) (piece cp3) let months be deducted from the contributory period, with the
-- pensionable earnings those months carry; subsection 56(4) is "subject to" them.
DECLARE `cp4 Earnings record for a disability pension` HAS
    `the disabled contributor's total pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of months in the disabled contributor's contributory period` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of those months deducted under subsections 48(2) and (4)` IS A NUMBER
    `the pensionable earnings attributable to the months so deducted` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Section 56(1) -- the basic monthly amount`

-- src:1621 | 56 (1) A disability pension payable to a contributor is a basic monthly amount consisting of
-- src:1622 | (a) a flat rate benefit, calculated as provided in subsection (2); and
-- src:1623 | (b) 75% of the amount of the contributor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated as the aggregate of
-- src:1624 | (i) the amount calculated as provided in subsection (3),
-- src:1625 | (ii) the amount calculated as provided in subsection (3.1), and
-- src:1626 | (iii) the amount calculated as provided in subsection (3.2).
@ref Act s 56(1) (src:1621-1626)
GIVEN `the flat rate benefit` IS A NUMBER
      portions IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 56(1) — the basic monthly amount of a disability pension` `the flat rate benefit` portions MEANS
    `the flat rate benefit` PLUS (75% TIMES (  portions's `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`
                                             PLUS portions's `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension`
                                             PLUS portions's `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension`))

§§ `Section 56(2) -- the flat rate benefit`

-- src:1627 | Calculation of flat rate benefit
-- src:1628 | (2) The amount of the flat rate benefit mentioned in paragraph (1)(a) is
-- src:1629 | (a) in the case of a flat rate benefit commencing to be payable for a month in the year 1986, ninety-one dollars and six cents;
-- src:1630 | (b) in the case of a flat rate benefit payable for a month in the year 1987, an amount calculated by multiplying
-- src:1631 | (i) two hundred and thirty-three dollars and thirty-eight cents
-- src:1632 | by
-- src:1633 | (ii) the ratio that the Pension Index for 1987 bears to the Pension Index for 1986; and
-- src:1634 | (c) in the case of a flat rate benefit commencing to be payable for a month in the year 1988 or any subsequent year, an amount calculated by multiplying
-- src:1635 | (i) the amount of the flat rate benefit that would have been payable for a month in the year preceding that year
-- src:1636 | by
-- src:1637 | (ii) the ratio that the Pension Index for the year in which the benefit commences to be payable bears to the Pension Index for the year preceding that year.
@ref Act s 56(2) (src:1627-1637)
GIVEN `the year in which the flat rate benefit commences to be payable` IS A NUMBER
      `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 56(2) — the flat rate benefit of a disability pension` `the year in which the flat rate benefit commences to be payable` `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the year in which the flat rate benefit commences to be payable` EQUALS 1986
            THEN JUST 91.06
        IF `the year in which the flat rate benefit commences to be payable` EQUALS 1987
            THEN `cp4 an amount that may be missing times a ratio that may be missing` (JUST 233.38) (`cp4 the ratio of the Pension Index for a year to the Pension Index for the year before` 1987 `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986`)
        IF `the year in which the flat rate benefit commences to be payable` AT LEAST 1988
            THEN `cp4 an amount that may be missing times a ratio that may be missing` (`s 56(2) — the flat rate benefit of a disability pension` (`the year in which the flat rate benefit commences to be payable` MINUS 1) `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986`) (`cp4 the ratio of the Pension Index for a year to the Pension Index for the year before` `the year in which the flat rate benefit commences to be payable` `the Pension Index by year, beginning with 1986`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Section 56(3), (3.1) and (3.2) -- the three portions of the retirement pension`

-- src:1638 | Calculation for purpose of subparagraph (1)(b)(i)
-- src:1639 | (3) The amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension that is to be used for the purpose of subparagraph (1)(b)(i) is equal to 25% of their average monthly pensionable earnings calculated as provided in subsections (4) and (5).
@ref Act s 56(3) (src:1638-1639)
GIVEN `the year in which the contributor is deemed to have become disabled` IS A NUMBER
      earnings IS A `cp4 Earnings record for a disability pension`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 56(3) — the base portion of the contributor's retirement pension` `the year in which the contributor is deemed to have become disabled` earnings MEANS
    -- Subsections (4) and (4.1) give the average only for a contributor deemed disabled in 1997 or later;
    -- for an earlier year the text gives none (NOTES.md, fork register).
    BRANCH
        IF `the year in which the contributor is deemed to have become disabled` AT LEAST 1998
            THEN JUST (25% TIMES `s 56(4) — the average monthly pensionable earnings of a contributor deemed disabled after 1997` earnings)
        IF `the year in which the contributor is deemed to have become disabled` EQUALS 1997
            THEN JUST (25% TIMES `s 56(4.1) — the average monthly pensionable earnings of a contributor deemed disabled in 1997` earnings)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1640 | Calculation for purpose of subparagraph (1)(b)(ii)
-- src:1641 | (3.1) The amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension that is to be used for the purpose of subparagraph (1)(b)(ii) is equal to 8.33% of their first additional monthly pensionable earnings calculated as provided in subsection (4.01).
@ref Act s 56(3.1) (src:1640-1641)
GIVEN `the first additional monthly pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 56(3.1) — the first additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension` `the first additional monthly pensionable earnings` MEANS
    8.33% TIMES `the first additional monthly pensionable earnings`

-- src:1642 | Calculation for purpose of subparagraph (1)(b)(iii)
-- src:1643 | (3.2) The amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension that is to be used for the purpose of subparagraph (1)(b)(iii) is equal to 33.33% of the contributor’s second additional monthly pensionable earnings calculated as provided in subsection (4.02).
@ref Act s 56(3.2) (src:1642-1643)
GIVEN `the second additional monthly pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 56(3.2) — the second additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension` `the second additional monthly pensionable earnings` MEANS
    33.33% TIMES `the second additional monthly pensionable earnings`

§§ `Section 56(4) and (4.1) -- average monthly pensionable earnings`

-- src:1644 | Average monthly pensionable earnings
-- src:1645 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3), the average monthly pensionable earnings of a contributor who is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of this Act after December 31, 1997 is, subject to subsections 48(2) and (4), the amount obtained by dividing
-- src:1646 | (a) the contributor’s total pensionable earnings
-- src:1647 | by
-- src:1648 | (b) the total number of months in the contributor’s contributory period or 48, whichever is greater.
@ref Act s 56(4) (src:1644-1648)
GIVEN earnings IS A `cp4 Earnings record for a disability pension`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 56(4) — the average monthly pensionable earnings of a contributor deemed disabled after 1997` earnings MEANS
    ((earnings's `the disabled contributor's total pensionable earnings`) MINUS (earnings's `the pensionable earnings attributable to the months so deducted`))
        DIVIDED BY (max ((earnings's `the number of months in the disabled contributor's contributory period`) MINUS (earnings's `the number of those months deducted under subsections 48(2) and (4)`)) 48)

-- src:1657 | Average monthly pensionable earnings
-- src:1658 | (4.1) For the purposes of subsection (3), the average monthly pensionable earnings of a contributor who is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of this Act in 1997 is, subject to subsections 48(2) and (4), the amount obtained by dividing
-- src:1659 | (a) the contributor’s total pensionable earnings
-- src:1660 | by
-- src:1661 | (b) the total number of months in the contributor’s contributory period or 24, whichever is greater.
@ref Act s 56(4.1) (src:1657-1661)
GIVEN earnings IS A `cp4 Earnings record for a disability pension`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 56(4.1) — the average monthly pensionable earnings of a contributor deemed disabled in 1997` earnings MEANS
    ((earnings's `the disabled contributor's total pensionable earnings`) MINUS (earnings's `the pensionable earnings attributable to the months so deducted`))
        DIVIDED BY (max ((earnings's `the number of months in the disabled contributor's contributory period`) MINUS (earnings's `the number of those months deducted under subsections 48(2) and (4)`)) 24)

§§ `Section 56(4.01) and (4.02) -- first and second additional monthly pensionable earnings`

-- src:1649 | First additional monthly pensionable earnings
-- src:1650 | (4.01) For the purpose of subsection (3.1), a contributor’s first additional monthly pensionable earnings are an amount calculated by
-- src:1651 | (a) in the case where their first additional contributory period is less than or equal to 480 months, dividing their total first additional pensionable earnings by 480; or
-- src:1652 | (b) in the case where their first additional contributory period exceeds 480 months, dividing the aggregate of their 480 highest first additional pensionable earnings for a month by 480.
@ref Act s 56(4.01) (src:1649-1652)
GIVEN `the first additional contributory period, in months` IS A NUMBER
      `the total first additional pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of the 480 highest first additional pensionable earnings for a month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 56(4.01) — the first additional monthly pensionable earnings` `the first additional contributory period, in months` `the total first additional pensionable earnings` `the aggregate of the 480 highest first additional pensionable earnings for a month` MEANS
    IF `the first additional contributory period, in months` AT MOST 480
    THEN `the total first additional pensionable earnings` DIVIDED BY 480
    ELSE `the aggregate of the 480 highest first additional pensionable earnings for a month` DIVIDED BY 480

-- src:1653 | Second additional monthly pensionable earnings
-- src:1654 | (4.02) For the purpose of subsection (3.2), a contributor’s second additional monthly pensionable earnings are an amount calculated by
-- src:1655 | (a) in the case where their second additional contributory period is less than or equal to 480 months, dividing their total second additional pensionable earnings by 480; or
-- src:1656 | (b) in the case where their second additional contributory period exceeds 480 months, dividing the aggregate of their 480 highest second additional pensionable earnings for a month by 480.
@ref Act s 56(4.02) (src:1653-1656)
GIVEN `the second additional contributory period, in months` IS A NUMBER
      `the total second additional pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of the 480 highest second additional pensionable earnings for a month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 56(4.02) — the second additional monthly pensionable earnings` `the second additional contributory period, in months` `the total second additional pensionable earnings` `the aggregate of the 480 highest second additional pensionable earnings for a month` MEANS
    IF `the second additional contributory period, in months` AT MOST 480
    THEN `the total second additional pensionable earnings` DIVIDED BY 480
    ELSE `the aggregate of the 480 highest second additional pensionable earnings for a month` DIVIDED BY 480

§§ `Section 56(5) -- the contributory period`

-- src:1662 | Contributory period
-- src:1663 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (4), the contributory period of a contributor is the period
-- src:1664 | (a) commencing January 1, 1966 or when he reaches eighteen years of age, whichever is the later, and
-- src:1665 | (b) ending with the month in which he is determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph 44(1)(b),
-- src:1666 | but excluding
-- src:1667 | (c) any month that was excluded from the contributor’s contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability, and
-- src:1668 | (d) in relation to any benefits payable under this Act for any month after December, 1977, any month for which the contributor was a family allowance recipient in a year for which the contributor’s base unadjusted pensionable earnings were equal to or less than the contributor’s basic exemption for the year.
@ref Act s 56(5) (src:1662-1668)
GIVEN `date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the month in which the contributor is determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph 44(1)(b)` IS A DATE
      `the month for which the benefit is payable` IS A DATE
      `the months excluded from the contributory period under this Act or a provincial pension plan by reason of disability` IS A NUMBER
      `the months for which the contributor was a family allowance recipient in a year for which the base unadjusted pensionable earnings were no more than the basic exemption` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 56(5) — the number of months in the contributory period` `date of birth` `the month in which the contributor is determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph 44(1)(b)` `the month for which the benefit is payable` `the months excluded from the contributory period under this Act or a provincial pension plan by reason of disability` `the months for which the contributor was a family allowance recipient in a year for which the base unadjusted pensionable earnings were no more than the basic exemption` MEANS
    max 0 ((`the months from the start of the period to its end, both counted` MINUS `the months excluded from the contributory period under this Act or a provincial pension plan by reason of disability`) MINUS `the months excluded under paragraph (d)`)
    WHERE
        -- (a): January 1966, or when he reaches eighteen, whichever is the later. Reaching an age goes
        -- through section 2(2): the 18th birthday is deemed reached at the start of the following month.
        `the date the contributor is deemed to reach eighteen` MEANS `s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `any other provision` `date of birth` 18
        `the start of the period` MEANS
            IF `the date the contributor is deemed to reach eighteen` AT LEAST (YMD 1966 1 1)
            THEN `the date the contributor is deemed to reach eighteen`
            ELSE YMD 1966 1 1
        -- (b): ending with the month in which he is determined to have become disabled. Both the first
        -- and the last month are counted.
        `the months from the start of the period to its end, both counted` MEANS
            IF `the month in which the contributor is determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph 44(1)(b)` AT LEAST (`the month of a date` `the start of the period`)
            THEN (`the number of months from the month of one date to the month of another` `the start of the period` `the month in which the contributor is determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph 44(1)(b)`) PLUS 1
            ELSE 0
        -- (d): only "in relation to any benefits payable under this Act for any month after December, 1977".
        `the months excluded under paragraph (d)` MEANS
            IF `the month for which the benefit is payable` AT LEAST (YMD 1978 1 1)
            THEN `the months for which the contributor was a family allowance recipient in a year for which the base unadjusted pensionable earnings were no more than the basic exemption`
            ELSE 0

§§ `Section 56(6) -- if a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings occurs`

-- src:1669 | If division of unadjusted pensionable earnings occurs
-- src:1670 | (6) The amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension that is to be used for the purpose of subparagraph (1)(b)(i), in the case of a contributor in respect of whom a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings takes place either before or after the commencement of the disability pension, if the division reduces the disability pension otherwise payable, is to be calculated by dividing
-- src:1671 | (a) the aggregate of
-- src:1672 | (i) the amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated in accordance with subsections (3), (4), (4.1) and (5) before the division, multiplied by the aggregate of
-- src:1673 | (A) the number of months that have been excluded from the contributor’s contributory period under this Act or a provincial pension plan by reason of disability, and
-- src:1674 | (B) the number of months remaining until the month in which the contributor reaches sixty-five years of age, and
-- src:1675 | (ii) the amount of the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension, which amount is calculated in accordance with subsections (3), (4), (4.1) and (5) following the division, multiplied by the number of months in the contributor’s contributory period calculated in accordance with subsection (5)
-- src:1676 | by
-- src:1677 | (b) the aggregate of
-- src:1678 | (i) the number of months that have been excluded from the contributor’s contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability,
-- src:1679 | (ii) the number of months remaining until the month in which the contributor reaches sixty-five years of age, and
-- src:1680 | (iii) the number of months in the contributor’s contributory period calculated in accordance with subsection (5).
@ref Act s 56(6) (src:1669-1680)
GIVEN `the division reduces the disability pension otherwise payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the portion calculated before the division` IS A NUMBER
      `the portion calculated following the division` IS A NUMBER
      `the months excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability` IS A NUMBER
      `the months remaining until the month in which the contributor reaches sixty-five years of age` IS A NUMBER
      `the months in the contributory period calculated in accordance with subsection (5)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 56(6) — the base portion of the retirement pension when a division reduces the disability pension` `the division reduces the disability pension otherwise payable` `the portion calculated before the division` `the portion calculated following the division` `the months excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability` `the months remaining until the month in which the contributor reaches sixty-five years of age` `the months in the contributory period calculated in accordance with subsection (5)` MEANS
    -- NOTHING: subsection (6) does not give the amount (it applies only if the division reduces the
    -- pension, and the divisor must not be zero); the subsection (3) amount then stands.
    IF (NOT `the division reduces the disability pension otherwise payable`) OR (`the divisor` EQUALS 0)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the dividend` DIVIDED BY `the divisor`)
    WHERE
        `the pre-division months` MEANS `the months excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability` PLUS `the months remaining until the month in which the contributor reaches sixty-five years of age`
        `the dividend` MEANS (`the portion calculated before the division` TIMES `the pre-division months`) PLUS (`the portion calculated following the division` TIMES `the months in the contributory period calculated in accordance with subsection (5)`)
        `the divisor` MEANS `the pre-division months` PLUS `the months in the contributory period calculated in accordance with subsection (5)`
